{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-121237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/state.json" "file_sha256" "d99c7956ea2ef1d67882e6e61d2d1178dfff2e667b5e1611b92fefa1688362ff"} {"question" "q-121237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $2{x}^{2}$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/7c851189a040934728e1b312706b4727c141cc678a4be870b6057e281be6e0fd.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/state.json" "file_sha256" "d99c7956ea2ef1d67882e6e61d2d1178dfff2e667b5e1611b92fefa1688362ff"} {"question" "q-121237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e58b44acdd9457c30fb264ff56c01c22fa69b4c1cd838665ce26ae9a216c301"} {"question" "q-121237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/state.json" "file_sha256" "d99c7956ea2ef1d67882e6e61d2d1178dfff2e667b5e1611b92fefa1688362ff"} {"question" "q-121237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/state.json" "file_sha256" "d99c7956ea2ef1d67882e6e61d2d1178dfff2e667b5e1611b92fefa1688362ff"} {"question" "q-121237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/state.json" "file_sha256" "d99c7956ea2ef1d67882e6e61d2d1178dfff2e667b5e1611b92fefa1688362ff"} {"question" "q-317187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$ Fill the table with appropriate sign of $f(x,y)$ as shown below.\n\n| $y>0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "